new file mode 100644
index 0000000..415f1f3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelogs/fragments/password_hash_bcrypt_ident.yml
@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@
+minor_changes:
+  - password_hash filter and password lookup - support selecting the BCrypt ident (``2``, ``2a``, ``2y``, or ``2b``)
diff --git a/docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_filters.rst b/docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_filters.rst
index d7907d1..4a5570a 100644
--- a/docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_filters.rst
+++ b/docs/docsite/rst/user_guide/playbooks_filters.rst
@@ -1335,6 +1335,13 @@ Some hash types allow providing a rounds parameter::
     {{ 'secretpassword' | password_hash('sha256', 'mysecretsalt', rounds=10000) }}
     # => "$5$rounds=10000$mysecretsalt$Tkm80llAxD4YHll6AgNIztKn0vzAACsuuEfYeGP7tm7"
 
+BCrypt hashes can select the identifier used in the hash. The supported values are ``2``, ``2a``, ``2y``, and ``2b``::
+
+    {{ 'secretpassword' | password_hash('bcrypt', ident='2a') }}
+    # => "$2a$12$..."
+
+When omitted, ``password_hash`` keeps the default of the installed hashing backend. The ``password`` lookup defaults to ``2a`` for BCrypt and saves the identifier with the salt.
+
 .. _other_useful_filters:
 
 Manipulating text
